   "conclusion": {
    "diagnosis": "CNC-03 has a genuine mechanical fault, most consistent with a bearing/spindle defect. Vibration jumped from ~0.003 mm/s at tick 70 to about 5.0–5.2 mm/s sustained across ticks 71–78, well above the 4.50 mm/s alarm threshold, then fell back to normal once the machine was stopped (E15). Before tick 70 vibration was normal (E5), nearby CNC-04 is normal (E14) ruling out an external source, and the readings are too sustained and consistent to be a sensor glitch (H2) or spurious alarm (H4). Following error also rose to ~1.8 µm during the event (E12) and power was elevated (E10), supporting an actual axis/mechanical problem rather than a reporting fault. CNC-03 is now idle and has no hydraulics (E3).",
